notes="Landscape music-paper sheet, two columns, headed EZ 2 and numbered360. It continues the equivariant Eilenberg-Zilber discussion, a resolution W_n, coherent commutativity examples and a construction headed operations de Steenrod. The arrow to Hom carries an angular question mark, and Hom has a prime, not an imposed grading bullet. The product argument is not completed with extra parentheses. The circled interval action, mapsto tail, sphere drawing, cancelled trials and separating strokes are retained. The group-operation glyph is an integral-shaped single S; its intended wreath-product role does not warrant replacing its ink by wr. The prose has ont ce and de chains. The chain target carries a small xi-like exponent; its mathematical meaning is not silently repaired. The initial cohomological/cocycle capital is overwritten and remains Z^n or H^n. The construction starts with W_p but labels equivariance and cohomology by Sigma_n; only the final K and group-cohomology formulas switch to Sigma_p. These inconsistencies are preserved. If f is represented by a degree-n cocycle and lambda is a chain map, then f tensor p has degree pn and zero differential, so composition with multiplication yields a degree-pn cocycle. This is only a conditional degree/differential check. Equivariance also depends on the permutation signs and the action on A[pn], which are not specified here; no construction theorem or Kunneth assertion is certified. The coefficient ring is stated only to have characteristic p, while the last tensor product is over F_p and suppresses coefficients on the group factor. No outside Steenrod reference was consulted. No date."
